# What jxa.lua needs from outside Hammerspoon, declared beside the only file that knows
# this tool exists. Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason.
# See Dependencies.spoon for the kinds and for how these files are found.
#
# The system kind, a binary at a fixed absolute path rather than something found on PATH,
# so the locator is the path and the file keeps that same literal. Nothing is injected,
# the declaration exists so the manifest records what this spoon actually runs.
#
# Optional rather than required, because the root wires BrowserTabs unconditionally and
# required would claim a refusal that never happens. It ships with macOS.
osascript | system | /usr/bin/osascript | optional | runs the JXA that asks each browser for its open tabs
